      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "STORM VENDETTA (5) is racing in fine form, putting two wins together. Scored from this barrier at Melton then had enough speed to cross and lead from a very wide draw before digging deep for a dogged win at Ballarat last week. Facing a tougher assignment but he is going well enough to take that step. TED NZ (7) has been good in two Melton outings off a very long spell, placing fresh before working hard but sticking on to go under by 5m last time. Draws out again but his fitness is building so he could be ready to strike. POSTERIZED (1) didn't do a bad job when fourth from wider here last time out. Came from the back row to miss by a nose at Melton prior. Should get every chance from the ace draw. ANGELS WATCHING (3) draws well again and could be close to a win after two successive placings, the latest a third at Geelong.",
